# SIIFMART Project Rules

Follow root `AGENTS.md`; `.agent/RULES.md` is the detailed index. Keep changes consistent with the focused guides.

- Inspect `git status --short` before code edits and preserve uncommitted work.
- Split files over 500 lines before changing them. Run the project type check after code changes.
- Enforce authorization, site scope, and country scope at trusted server/database boundaries.
- Keep country-specific settings and data isolated; only authorized executives see the central country switch.
- UI writes use hooks and services. Validate inputs, use explicit database field allowlists, propagate errors, and log safely.
- Create a persistent migration before writing or proposing SQL. Do not apply without authorization; provide the full SQL and application status in the final response.
- Use shared design tokens and accessible patterns. Profile before optimizing; avoid speculative memoization or fixed list thresholds.
- Preserve approvals, blind counts, audit records, and chain-of-custody controls. Do not expose secrets or sensitive data.
- Keep source and guidance files under 500 lines. Summarize outcomes in plain language.
